`el("td", null, pill(...))` — my `el` sets textContent when given a non-string node → `String(node)` = "[object HTMLSpanElement]". Need to append the node instead. Fix `el` to appendChild when value is a Node.

Update el():
```js
function el(tag, cls, value) {
  const node = document.createElement(tag);
  if (cls) node.className = cls;
  if (value !== undefined) node.appendChild(value && value.nodeType ? value : document.createTextNode(String(value)));
  return node;
}
```
That makes pill(text, cls) usage consistent.

